{"name":"Imperial Dynasty","hex":"#33746b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"imperial","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Related to an empire, emperor, or empress.","Relating to the British imperial system of measurement."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bottle of wine (usually Bordeaux) containing 6 liters of fluid, eight times the volume of a standard bottle.","A writing paper size measuring 30 × 22 inches, or printing paper measuring 32 × 22 inches."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imperial"},{"term":"dynasty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A series of rulers or dynasts from one family.","A family considered over time, with its ancestors and descendants"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dynasty"}],"entries":[{"title":"Imperial Dynasty (restaurant)","blocks":[{"text":"The Imperial Dynasty restaurant was a gourmet restaurant in Hanford, California. The restaurant was founded in 1883 in Hanford's Chinatown, and was run by the same family for four generations, having started as a simple noodle house in the 19th century."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperial_Dynasty_(restaurant)","wikidata":"Q14682460"},{"title":"Dynasty","blocks":[{"text":"A dynasty is a sequence of rulers from the same family, usually in the context of a monarchical system, but sometimes also appearing in republics. A \"house\" is an imperial, royal or noble family, not always ruling. \nHistorians periodize the histories of many states and civilizations, such as the Roman Empire, Imperial Iran, Ancient Egypt (3100–30 BCE), and Ancient and Imperial China, using a framework of successive dynasties. As such, the term \"dynasty\" may be used to delimit the era during which a family reigned."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/The_Imperial_Family_of_Japan%2C_2021.jpg/330px-The_Imperial_Family_of_Japan%2C_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynasty","wikidata":"Q164950"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Order_of_the_Civil_Merit_Ceremony._5th_Felipe_VI_Reign_Anniversary_02_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Order_of_the_Civil_Merit_Ceremony._5th_Felipe_VI_Reign_Anniversary_02_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Order_of_the_Civil_Merit_Ceremony._5th_Felipe_VI_Reign_Anniversary_02_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Order_of_the_Civil_Merit_Ceremony._5th_Felipe_VI_Reign_Anniversary_02_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Spanish royal family of the House of Bourbon dates its roots to the Capetian dynasty of the 9th century, thus making it the oldest still reigning dynasty in Europe (photograph of King Felipe VI, Queen Letizia, the Princess of Asturias and her younger sister Infanta Sofía, in 2019)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrder_of_the_Civil_Merit_Ceremony._5th_Felipe_VI_Reign_Anniversary_02_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Maria_Theresia_im_Kreise_ihrer_Familie.jpg/500px-Maria_Theresia_im_Kreise_ihrer_Familie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Maria_Theresia_im_Kreise_ihrer_Familie.jpg/500px-Maria_Theresia_im_Kreise_ihrer_Familie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Family portrait of Empress Maria Theresa of the Habsburg dynasty, surrounded by her children who were married into various European dynasties. Marriage policy amongst dynasties led to the Pax Austriaca.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaria_Theresia_im_Kreise_ihrer_Familie.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Welcome_for_